 "notes": [
  "Run-on (a convention: water flowing onto an area from upslope) is the volume entering the square across its edges; inflow and outflow per edge are integrated per 50 m piece and 10 s output step, so both are lower bounds of the gross fluxes and their difference is exact.",
  "Both runs have the same rain on the square: the ring's forcing keeps every pixel of the square run's forcing file and adds pixels around it by the same nearest-cell rule.",
  "The ring's outer edge is an outflow boundary on land, as F3's: run-on from beyond 500 m is still left out."
 ],
